    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This spacious four bedroom detached bungalow occupies a generous c. garden site and extends to approximately c. 131.2 sq.m. The accommodation comprises an Entrance Hall, Living Room, Sitting Room, Kitchen, Utility Room, Guest W.C., Four Bedrooms, and a Family Bathroom. \n\nOutside, the property enjoys extensive gardens to the front and rear, together with a range of useful outbuildings, including a block-built storage shed and a greenhouse. \n\nWhile this property requires upgrading, it may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the purchaser meeting the relevant eligibility criteria.\n\nSituated on the popular Gardenrath Road, approximately 1km from Kells town centre, this property offers the benefit of excellent outdoor space while remaining within easy reach of all local amenities. Schools, shops, sporting facilities, and everyday services are all conveniently accessible, while the nearby M3 motorway provides an excellent commuter route to Dublin.\n\nThe property`s generous grounds, mature setting, and established outbuildings offer excellent potential for those seeking additional space in a convenient and well regarded location.\n\nThe bungalow`s heating system was upgraded approx. 3 years ago including new radiators, immersion and hot tank and is double glazed.\n\nLOCATION \nThe property is located near Kells town centre and within easy access to the M3/M50. There are excellent schools both primary and secondary within walking distance. Kells is a heritage town with many sporting facilities to include golf, swimming, football; award winning restaurants, shops, hotel, pubs and a thriving local community. The Hinterland Book Festival and the Samhain Festival of Food Culture are located in Kells and are examples of what`s on offer locally.\n\nHall\nTo front.\n\nLiving Room\nOpen fire in stone fireplace, connected to a back boiler. Wooden flooring. Double doorway to Kitchen/Dining Room.\n\nSitting Room\nLarge window overlooking the front garden. Laminate flooring. Open fire (connected for back boiler).\n\nKitchen/Dining\nTo rear. Fitted shaker style kitchen. Solid Fuel stove. Dual aspect room. Doors to utility and Sitting Room.\n\nUtility\nPlumbed with door to the back garden. Large space with easy access to the Guest W.C.\n\nGuest W.C.\nW.c. and w.h.b.\n\nBedroom 1\nTo rear.\n\nBedroom 2\nTo front. Carpeted and storage.\n\nBedroom 3\nTo rear. Laminate flooring and storage.\n\nBedroom 4\nTo front.\n\nBathroom\nRecently refurbished. Wet room, shower, w.h.b. and w.c.\n\nHotpress\nNew tank and immersion.\n\nOutdoors\nLarge back garden with access to the front and side. Site c. 0.7 acres. Out buildings - Greenhouse, shed (block built), coal shed and storage shed.\n\n\nDirections\nFrom Rockfield Road (R164), turn left onto Gardenrath Rd Lower and the property will be on the left. Follow eircode A82 V3V8.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious 4 bedroom detached bungalow c. 131.2 sq.m.\nMay qualify for Vacant Property Refurbishment grant subject to eligibility.\nMature, established setting. \nLocated c. 1km from Kells town centre\nEasy access to M3/M50 commuter route to Dublin.\nWalking distance to primary & secondary schools.\nExtensive front and rear gardens. \nBlock-built storage shed & greenhouse.\nHeating system upgraded approx. 3 years ago (radiators, hot water cylinder & immersion).\nExcellent selection of shops, restaurants, sport & leisure facilities nearby."
      }
